   "source": [
    "# Initial data observations overview:\n",
    " - Dataset contains 9994 records and 21 features\n",
    " - There are no missing values in the features\n",
    " - High cardinality columns like Row ID, Order ID, Customer ID, Customer Name, Postal Code and Product ID are not useful for analysis and can be dropped\n",
    " - The Order Date and Ship Date columns should be converted to datetime format for time based analysis\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0794ba6f-dfa8-4aee-bc91-0b002e2ca37f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# STEP 5: Data Cleaning"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a74c147c-4d0e-4460-8160-de1472b985e2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# convert date_added to date_time format\n",
    "df['Order Date'] = pd.to_datetime(df['Order Date'], errors='coerce')\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "df['Ship Date'] = pd.to_datetime(df['Ship Date'], errors='coerce')\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "#drop columns \n",
    "df.drop(['Row ID', 'Order ID', 'Customer ID', 'Customer Name', 'Postal Code', 'Product ID'], axis=1, inplace = True)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cfb909bd-7417-46c4-b211-9553e02eb759",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# STEP 6: Feature Engineering"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "efa7b847-216a-4435-8e85-bcec6566c751",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# order date - tear, month, quarter\n",
    "df['order_year'] = df['Order Date'].dt.year\n",
    "df['order_month'] = df['Order Date'].dt.month_name()\n",
    "df['order_quarter'] = df['Order Date'].dt.quarter\n",
    "\n",
    "#  average shipping time\n",
    "df['shipping_days'] =  (df['Ship Date']- df['Order Date']).dt.days\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6100d19f-d4bb-416d-b0fe-9b3f85cb1a9b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# STEP 7: Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5b132e4c-00ac-4c9d-8761-8c851bda49d5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Business Questions\n",
    "- What are the Sales Analysis over Region, State, Segement?\n",
    "- What are the Sales trends over time?\n",
    "- Profit Analysis\n",
    "- Discount Analysis\n",
    "- What are Category Insights for sales and profits?\n",
    "- What are the Products-level Insights for sales?\n",
    "- How much is the average Shipping days?\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3860a08b-34fc-4227-b9e5-f2c9ade71cf2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "import matplotlib.colors as mcolors\n",
    "list(mcolors.CSS4_COLORS.keys())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "793e28c2-3146-41fc-93e4-ccc7bfe64131",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "## Sales Analysis over Region, State, Segement\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot 1: Sales distribution by Region\n",
    "region_by_sales = df.groupby('Region')['Sales'].sum()\n",
    "region_by_sales.plot(kind = 'bar', color='teal')\n",
    "plt.title(\"Sales distribution by Region\", fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Region\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Sales in Dollars\")\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "#Insight: Sales in the West Region are high than other regions. \n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot 2: top 10 states\n",
    "top_states = df.groupby('State')['Sales'].sum().sort_values(ascending=False).head(10)\n",
    "top_states.plot(kind='bar', color='indigo')\n",
    "plt.title(\"Top 10 State Sales\", fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"States\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Sales in Dollars\")\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot 3: Sales by Segment\n",
    "segment_by_state = df.groupby('Segment')['Sales'].sum()\n",
    "segment_by_state.plot(kind = 'bar', color='dodgerblue')\n",
    "plt.title(\"Sales distribution by Segment\", fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Segment\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Sales\")\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "#Insight: Consumer has more sales than corporate and homeoffice\n",
    "\n",
    "## Profit Analysis \n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot 4: Profit Analysis\n",
    "sns.histplot(df['Profit'], bins=20, kde=True, color='blueviolet')\n",
    "plt.title(\"Profit Distribution\", fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "#Insight: Profit distribution is highly skewed with significant negative values, indicating frequent losses.\n",
    "\n",
    "sns.boxplot(x='Profit',data = df)\n",
    "plt.title(\"Profit Distribution to identify outliers\", fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot 5: Profit distribution by Region\n",
    "profit_by_region = df.groupby('Region')['Profit'].sum()\n",
    "profit_by_region.plot(kind = 'bar', color='palevioletred')\n",
    "plt.title(\"Profit distribution by Region\", fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Region\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Profit\")\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "#Insight: East and West Regions has more Profit margins than other Regions\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot 6: Profit distribution by State\n",
    "profit_by_state = df.groupby('State')['Profit'].sum()\n",
    "top_profit_states = profit_by_state.sort_values(ascending=False).head(10)\n",
    "top_profit_states.plot(kind = 'bar', color='forestgreen')\n",
    "plt.title(\"Top profit states\", fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"States\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Profit\")\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "#Insight: California, New York, Texas and Washington has moreprofit margin than other states. Ohio, Texas, Pensylvania and Illinois have more losses.\n",
    "\n",
    "profit_by_state = df.groupby('State')['Profit'].sum()\n",
    "loss_states = profit_by_state.sort_values().head(10)\n",
    "loss_states.plot(kind = 'bar')\n",
    "plt.title(\"Loss states profit\", fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"States\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Profit\")\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Profit Margin feature\n",
    "df['profit_margin'] = (df['Profit'] / df['Sales']) * 100\n",
    "category_margin = df.groupby('Category')['profit_margin'].mean()\n",
    "category_margin.plot(kind = 'bar')\n",
    "plt.title(\"Profit Margin\", fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot 7: Discount Analysis\n",
    "sns.histplot(df['Discount'], bins=20, kde=True, color='green')\n",
    "plt.title(\"Discount Distribution\", fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "#Insight: zero discount have more sales?\n",
    "\n",
    "sns.boxplot(x='Discount',data = df)\n",
    "plt.title(\"Discount Distribution to identify outliers\", fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot 8: Discount Vs Profit\n",
    "sns.scatterplot(x= 'Discount', y='Profit', data = df)\n",
    "sns.scatterplot(\n",
    "    x='Discount',\n",
    "    y='Profit',\n",
    "    data=df,\n",
    "    alpha=0.5\n",
    ")\n",
    "plt.title(\"Discount VS Profit\", fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "#Insight: Higher discounts are strongly associated with lower profits and even losses, indicating aggressive discounting impacts profitability.\n",
    "#Higher discounts significantly reduce profitability and often lead to losses.\n",
    "\n",
    "loss_df = df[df['Profit'] < 0]\n",
    "loss_by_category = loss_df.groupby('Category')['Profit'].sum()\n",
    "loss_by_category.plot(kind='bar', color='red')\n",
    "plt.title(\"Loss by Category\")\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "#Insight: Furniture category contributes most to losses.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Sales trends over time\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot 9: Yearly Sales\n",
    "yearly_sales = df.groupby('order_year')['Sales'].sum() \n",
    "yearly_sales.plot(kind='bar', color='brown')\n",
    "plt.title(\"Yearly Sales Trend\", fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Year\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Sales\")\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "#Insight: 2017 has more sales\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot 10: Monthly Sales\n",
    "month_order = [ 'January','February','March','April','May','June', 'July','August','September','October','November','December']\n",
    "monthly_sales = df.groupby('order_month')['Sales'].sum().reindex(month_order)\n",
    "monthly_sales.plot(kind='line', marker='o', color='darkseagreen')\n",
    "plt.title(\"Monthly Sales Trend\", fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Month\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Sales\")\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "#Insight: November has more sales\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot 11: Quarterly Sales\n",
    "quarterly_sales = df.groupby('order_quarter')['Sales'].sum() \n",
    "quarterly_sales.plot(kind='bar', color='darkslateblue')\n",
    "plt.title(\"Quarterly Sales Trend\", fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Quarter\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Sales\")\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "#Insight: Quarter 4 has more sales\n",
    "\n",
    "## Category-Level Insights\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot 12: Sales by Category\n",
    "category_sales = df.groupby('Category')['Sales'].sum()\n",
    "category_sales.plot(kind = 'bar', color='burlywood')\n",
    "plt.title(\"Sales by Category\", fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Category\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Sales\")\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "#Insight: Technology has more sales\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot 13: Profit by Category\n",
    "category_profit = df.groupby('Category')['Profit'].sum()\n",
    "category_profit.plot(kind = 'bar', color='cadetblue')\n",
    "plt.title(\"Profit by Category\", fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Category\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Profit\")\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "# Insight: Technology has more sales and more profit\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "## Product-Level Insights\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot 14: Top Products by Sales\n",
    "products = df.groupby('Product Name')['Sales'].sum()\n",
    "top10_products = products.sort_values(ascending=False).head(10).sort_values()\n",
    "top10_products.plot(kind = 'barh', color = 'chartreuse')\n",
    "plt.title(\"Top Products by Sales\", fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Sales\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Products\")\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "#Insights: compact refrigerators and envelopes sales are popular\n",
    "\n",
    "## Shipping Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot 15: Average shipping days by Shipping mode\n",
    "shipping_analysis = df.groupby('Ship Mode')['shipping_days'].mean()\n",
    "shipping_analysis.plot(kind='bar', color = 'chocolate')\n",
    "plt.title(\"Average shipping days by Shipping mode\", fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Shipping Mode\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Shipping Days\")\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "#Insight: Same day is the fastest shipping fastest.Average shipping days will be 3 days.\n",
    "\n",
    "# shipping profit\n",
    "\n",
    "shipping_profit = df.groupby('Ship Mode')['Profit'].mean()\n",
    "shipping_profit.plot(kind='bar', color = 'chocolate')\n",
    "plt.title(\"Shipping Profit\", fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
